---
layout: base.njk
---

{#- Screen 2f, the page every blog post is drawn on. Sarah never opens this file:
    she writes a Markdown file in src/posts, and Eleventy pours it into the content
    slot below. posts.json points every file in that folder here.

    layout: base.njk, so the header, the dark footer and the four stylesheets come
    from the same shell every other page uses. No contactFooter, which is what
    gives a post the compact footer the design draws rather than the homepage's
    full contact block.

    Only two of the post's three front matter fields are read here. description
    never appears on the page — base.njk puts it in the meta tag, and blog.njk
uses it as the card excerpt on 2e. -#}
<div class="post-head">
    <a class="post-head__back" href="/blog/">← All posts</a>
    {#- The same two filters in the same order as the card on 2e, so the date on the
      index and the date on the post cannot drift apart: postDate gives the
      design's "12 Aug 2026", isoDate the datetime attribute a machine reads.

       -#}
    <time class="post-head__meta" datetime="{{ page.date | isoDate }}">{{ page.date | postDate }}</time>
    <h1 class="post-head__title">{{ title }}</h1>
</div>
{#- Sarah's Markdown, untouched. Everything inside is styled by tag name in
    pages.css: markdown-it emits plain p, h2, ul and blockquote with no classes
    on them, so this is the one block on the site with nothing to hook onto. -#}
<div class="post-body">{{ content | safe }}</div>
{#- The periwinkle block the design closes 2f with. A p rather than a heading:
    it is a line of marketing copy, and an h2 here would sit in the document
    outline among Sarah's real subheadings and be read as part of her article.

    /book/, like every "Book a consultation" on the site. The email address lives
    on that page alone, so when Sarah's arrives only book.njk changes. -#}
<div class="post-cta">
    <p class="post-cta__heading">Want a second pair of eyes on your CV?</p>
    <a class="post-cta__button" href="/book/">Book a consultation</a>
</div>
